From 2297d02d46ff799ef9aac2c47cfe8b1a1ebc8d8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rivian <rivianp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 02:59:04 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] photon: reply-target patch also extends the iMessage
 message schema (core strips unknown extras)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Task 1's rewrite put `replyTo` on the provider's raw record, and it never
arrived. Spectrum core rebuilds every message through
`extractExtras(raw, definition)`, which ends in
`definition.message.schema.parse(extra)`; the iMessage platform's schema is a
plain `z.object({...})`, so zod dropped the key it had not been told about.
Three tapped replies in a live run produced no linkage at all.

So the patch gains a second anchor — the provider's `messageSchema`
declaration, which now names a `replyTo` shape — and idempotency moves from
one file-level marker to one probe per rewrite. That second part is not
cosmetic: the production dist already carries Task 1's rewrite and its marker,
and a marker gate would call that done and leave the schema stripping `replyTo`
forever. Each rewrite now applies when its anchor is there, stands down when
its own comment is there, and throws when it finds neither.
