 strings before the schema sees them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The schema the last commit added types `threadRootId` and `part` as
`z.string()`, and `buildMessageBase` was handing them over exactly as the
provider gave them. A non-string from `@photon-ai/advanced-imessage` would not
have quietly dropped the linkage — `schema.parse` throws inside
`extractExtras`, taking the whole message with it. Apple sends
`threadOriginatorPart` as a string like `0:0:0`, but nothing in the provider
promises that, so the helper no longer depends on it.

`id` keeps the raw guid: it is the one required field, and a non-string there
should be loud rather than papered over.
